# gtc_v2_sim

Minimal GTC v2 case folder for running the ITG Cyclone base case as a
nonlinear electrostatic ion-temperature-gradient calculation with the zonal
mode enabled (`mode00=1`).

Build:

```sh
make
make c
```

Run the default short nonlinear case:

```sh
./run_itg_cyclone_base_nonlinear_zonal.sh
```

Useful runtime overrides:

```sh
MPI_NP=10 MSTEP=1000 MSNAP=10 CASE_DIR=itg_run_1000 ./run_itg_cyclone_base_nonlinear_zonal.sh
```

C/OpenMP hybrid runtime:

```sh
GTC_LAYOUT=auto GTC_CORES=10 MZETAMAX=16 ./run_itg_cyclone_base_nonlinear_zonal_c.sh
GTC_LAYOUT=omp GTC_CORES=10 MZETAMAX=37 ./run_itg_cyclone_base_nonlinear_zonal_c.sh
GTC_LAYOUT=mpi GTC_CORES=10 MZETAMAX=16 ./run_itg_cyclone_base_nonlinear_zonal_c.sh
GTC_LAYOUT=manual MPI_NP=2 OMP_NUM_THREADS=5 MZETAMAX=16 ./run_itg_cyclone_base_nonlinear_zonal_c.sh
MPI_NP=2 OMP_NUM_THREADS=5 MZETAMAX=16 ./run_itg_cyclone_base_nonlinear_zonal_c.sh
```

`GTC_LAYOUT=auto` chooses one unified MPI/OpenMP layout, including the two
endpoints: single-rank multi-thread (`omp`) and multi-rank single-thread
(`mpi`). Automatic layouts use an MPI rank count that divides `MZETAMAX`, so
the requested number of toroidal planes is preserved. When `GTC_LAYOUT` is set,
it owns the layout decision; use `GTC_LAYOUT=manual` for explicit
`MPI_NP`/`OMP_NUM_THREADS` runs.

For C runs, nonlinear full-n cases write only `nmode` mode selections. `mmode`
is written only for linear selected-mode runs (`NONLINEAR<0.5` and
`SPECTRUM_MODE=1`), where the history diagnostics need paired `(n,m)` modes.

Set `KEEP_RESTART=1` if you want to retain restart files. They are removed by
default to keep the case folder small.

Main outputs in the case directory:

- `history.out`: scalar and mode-amplitude history
- `sheareb.out`: zonal-flow/shearing diagnostics
- `snap*.out`: profile and field snapshots
- `summary.csv`: quick run summary
- `plots/`: generated figures when Python plotting dependencies are present
